{
  "_readme": [
    "Bibliographic source of truth for the Darśana branch of DGE (Nyāya, Vaiśeṣika, Mīmāṃsā).",
    "",
    "This file is the DUMP that code consumes. tools/darshanas/scaffold_darshanas.py reads it",
    "and generates: the folder tree under dge/data/darshana/, every _meta.json, empty",
    "data.json stubs with the right schema and default_author, the taxonomy.json subtree, and",
    "library.json entries. Nothing in the tree is hand-authored — edit this file and re-run.",
    "",
    "EVERY entry carries a 'verification' field. Only 'verified' entries have a URL in",
    "'evidence'. 'plausible' means structurally consistent with verified siblings but not",
    "individually catalogued; 'uncertain' means the attribution is actively in doubt. Nothing",
    "here is asserted without a status — that distinction is the point of the file.",
    "",
    "MODELLING DECISION — the vāda texts. Pañcalakṣaṇī, Siddhāntalakṣaṇa, Sāmānyanirukti,",
    "Avayava, Pakṣatā, Avacchedakatānirukti and the rest are NOT independent works. They are",
    "named topical sections of Tattvacintāmaṇi's Anumāna-khaṇḍa that circulate as printed",
    "extracts bundled with Dīdhiti + Jāgadīśī / Gādādharī. 'Pañcalakṣaṇī of Jagadīśa' and",
    "'Pañcalakṣaṇī of Gadādhara' are the SAME section at two commentary layers, not two works.",
    "So they are modelled as topic × layer: kind='vada' with a layer folder per commentary.",
    "Only Vyutpattivāda and Śaktivāda are genuinely standalone Gadādhara treatises, and",
    "Bādhānta is Rucidatta's at the Āloka layer — all three are filed as ordinary works.",
    "",
    "LAYER. 0 = mūla. 1 = commentary on the mūla. 2 = commentary on a layer-1 text. 3 = gloss",
    "on a layer-2 text. The folder tree is deliberately FLAT (all commentaries sit as sibling",
    "layer folders under their root work) — the true genealogy lives in 'comments_on' here, so",
    "a 4th-order gloss does not produce a 4-deep directory. This matches the mula/tika/tippani",
    "convention already used in dge/data/sarvamoola_grantha/."
  ],

